  "goal": "Land on the stage from the ledge with invincibility left",
  "why": "Hanging from the ledge makes {char} invincible for a short time, and the count keeps running after {char} lets go. A ledgedash gets {char} standing on the stage while some of it is left, so {char} can attack or grab an opponent waiting at the ledge without being hit.",
  "tutorial": {
    "camera": {
      "follow": "player",
      "distance": 140,
      "height": 10
    },
    "what": "A ledgedash is a let-go from the ledge, a double jump on the next frame, and an air dodge onto the stage as soon as {char} is above it, on frame {LD}. {char} lands with 10 frames of landing lag and invincibility left from the ledge.",
    "expect": "Each ledgedash is judged 60 frames after the let-go: how soon {char} double jumped, whether the air dodge landed on the stage, and whether invincibility was left after the landing lag. After misses, the coach shows your inputs frame by frame.",
    "example": [
      {
        "stick": [
          0,
          -1
        ],
        "frame": 1,
        "hold": 1
      },
      {
        "press": "jump",
        "frame": 2,
        "hold": 1
      },
      {
        "stick": [
          1,
          0
        ],
        "frame": 2,
        "hold": "LD-2"
      },
      {
        "stick": [
          0.7,
          -0.7
        ],
        "frame": "LD",
        "hold": 1
      },
      {
        "press": "R",
        "frame": "LD",
        "hold": 1
      }
    ],
    "marks": {
      "1": "Frame 1: stick down. {char} lets go of the ledge",
      "2": "Frame 2: X pressed, stick toward the stage. Double jump",
      "LD": "Frame {LD}: above the stage. R pressed, stick down and toward the stage",
      "LD+2": "Frame {f}: landing lag. Still invincible"
    },
    "lessons": [
      {
        "title": "Ledge invincibility",
        "text": [
          "Hanging from the ledge, {char} is invincible for 30 frames from the start of the hang. The count does not stop when {char} lets go, so each frame spent getting onto the stage uses it up.",
          "To let go, push the stick down or away from the stage. The game takes it only after one frame of the hang with the stick at rest. Then the double jump: press X or Y on the next frame, the first frame {char} can."
        ],
        "show": {
          "still": {
            "inputs": [
              {
                "stick": [
                  0,
                  -1
                ],
                "frame": 1,
                "hold": 1
              },
              {
                "press": "jump",
                "frame": 2,
                "hold": 1
              },
              {
                "stick": [
                  1,
                  0
                ],
                "frame": 2,
                "hold": "LD-2"
              },
              {
